// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Obsiddy — framework-tier schema
//
// `prisma.config.ts` points Prisma at the `prisma/schema` folder, so every
// `*.prisma` file in it is part of one schema. `framework-*.prisma` is the
// filename glob Sunrise reserves for a framework tier: Sunrise core never
// creates a file matching it, so this file merges cleanly on upgrade.
//
// Rules for everything added below (see .context/framework/obsiddy/plan.md):
//
//   - Every table is `@@map("framework_obsiddy_<name>")`. The prefix is what
//     keeps Obsiddy's tables from colliding with a host project's own.
//   - Every model carries `userId` and a `@@index([userId, …])` leading with
//     `userId` — D1. `ObsiddySpace` is the one satellite table holding a
//     hand-written FK to `"user"("id") ON DELETE CASCADE`; every other model
//     cascades from it, so GDPR erasure is transitive and no column is ever
//     added to `User`.
//   - The hand-written FK, the pgvector column, the HNSW index and the BM25
//     index are invisible to Prisma. Each needs a drift probe registered in
//     `lib/app/db-drift.ts`, or a later `migrate dev` will silently drop it.
//     Run `npm run db:drift-check` after every `migrate dev` — non-negotiable.
//
// Models land in phase 1. This file is intentionally empty until then: it
// exists from phase 0 so the schema glob, the migration path and the install
// checklist are proven before there is anything to lose.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
